<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>

<worksheet>
    <title>Quiz 7 - MTH 305 - Regan</title>

    <p>
        This quiz covers multiple equation ODE models, their fixed point(s), and
        stability and retakes on optimization of mathematical models and single
        equation ODE models, their fixed point(s), and stability.
        Read all <term>DIRECTIONS</term> carefully.
        Good luck!
    </p>

    <exercise workspace="2in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Find the fixed point(s) for the following system of differential
                equations.
                <md>
                    <mrow>
                    \frac{dx}{dt} \amp = x(y+1) - x^{2} \\
                    </mrow>
                    <mrow>
                    \frac{dy}{dt} \amp = y - 2xy \\
                     </mrow>
                </md>
            </p>

            <p>
                Determine the stability of one of the fixed points.
                Note: just need to state whether it is stable/unstable if you
                don't know specifics (e.g., spiral sink).
                Show all work.
            </p>

            <p>
                Remember, the stability is based on the eigenvalues of the
                Jacobian matrix
                <md>
                    \textrm{Jacobian,}\,\, J = \begin{bmatrix}\frac{\partial f}{\partial{x}} &amp; \frac{\partial f}{\partial{y}} \\  \\ \frac{\partial g}{\partial{x}} &amp; \frac{\partial g}{\partial{y}}\end{bmatrix},
                </md>
                where the trace, <m>T</m>, and determinant, <m>D</m>, give the
                eigenvalues of
                <md>
                    \lambda_{1}, \lambda_{2} = \frac{T \pm \sqrt{T^{2} - 4D}}{2}.
                </md>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    <exercise workspace="2in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Consider the following phase portrait with 4 plotted fixed
                points.
            </p>

            <image source="images/07quiz-1.png" width="60%">
                <shortdescription>
                    Graph of 4 fixed points and the phase portrait for a
                    competing species model.
                </shortdescription>
            </image>

            <p>
                Determine the stability of each of the four fixed points.
                Choose an initial condition that will end at a stable fixed
                point. Justify your responses.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    <p>
        <term>Retake of 1D ODE Models: </term>
    </p>

    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                Determine fixed point(s) and corresponding stability for the
                following differential equation.
                Show all work.
                <md>
                    \frac{dx}{dt} = 3x - x^{2}
                </md>
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>

    <p>
        <term>Last Retake of Optimization: </term>
    </p>

    <exercise workspace="1.5in">
        <statement>
            <p>
                We have 45 meters squared of material to build a box with a
                square base and no top.
                Determine the dimensions of the box that will maximize the
                enclosed volume.
            </p>
        </statement>
    </exercise>
</worksheet>